📂 Module 4.24.4 :  k-Fold Cross-Validation

  In machine learning, **k-Fold Cross-Validation** is a robust resampling technique used to evaluate the generalization ability of a predictive model. A simple train/test split (such as a single HoldOut validation) can sometimes result in optimistic or pessimistic performance estimates depending purely on how the data was randomly split.
In k-Fold Cross-Validation, the entire dataset is randomly partitioned into $k$ equal-sized subsets (folds). The model is then trained and tested $k$ times: in each iteration, a different fold is held out as the validation set while the remaining $k-1$ folds are used for training. By averaging the evaluation metrics across all $k$ iterations, you obtain a far more reliable, stable, and unbiased assessment of model performance.
Using k-Fold Cross-Validation ensures that every data point is used for both training and testing exactly once, minimizing variance caused by dataset splitting and offering a truer picture of how models like Decision Trees or Ensemble Bagging classifiers will perform on unseen real-world data.

Example Code :

% Load the tabular data from a CSV file
data = readtable('heart.csv');

% Extract all feature columns (from the first column up to the second-to-last column)
X = data(:, 1:end-1);

% Extract the target label column (last column) and convert it to an array
Y = table2array(data(:, end));

% Partition the dataset into a single 70% training and 30% testing HoldOut split
cv = cvpartition(Y, 'HoldOut', 0.3);
XTrain = X(training(cv), :);
YTrain = Y(training(cv));
XTest = X(test(cv), :);
YTest = Y(test(cv));

% Train a single Decision Tree on the HoldOut training set
modelTree = fitctree(XTrain, YTrain, 'MinLeafSize', 50, 'MaxNumSplits', 5);
predTree = predict(modelTree, XTest);
accTree_simple = mean(predTree == YTest);

% Train an Ensemble Bagging model on the HoldOut training set
modelEns = fitensemble(XTrain, YTrain, 'Method', 'Bag', 'NumLearningCycles', 10);
predEns = predict(modelEns, XTest);
accEns_simple = mean(predEns == YTest);

% Display performance metrics obtained from the single HoldOut split
fprintf('== HoldOut Results Without k-Fold ==\n\n');
fprintf('Decision Tree Accuracy: %.2f%%\n', accTree_simple * 100);
fprintf('Ensemble Learning Accuracy: %.2f%%\n', accEns_simple * 100);

% Define k = 10 for 10-fold cross-validation
k = 10;
cvp = cvpartition(Y, 'KFold', k);

% Preallocate arrays to store accuracy scores for each fold
accTree = zeros(k, 1);
accEns = zeros(k, 1);

% Perform 10-fold cross-validation loop
for i = 1:k
    % Train Decision Tree on k-1 folds and evaluate on the ith test fold
    mTree = fitctree(X(training(cvp, i), :), Y(training(cvp, i)), 'MinLeafSize', 50, 'MaxNumSplits', 5);
    pTree = predict(mTree, X(test(cvp, i), :));
    accTree(i) = mean(pTree == Y(test(cvp, i)));

    % Train Ensemble Bagging model on k-1 folds and evaluate on the ith test fold
    mEns = fitensemble(X(training(cvp, i), :), Y(training(cvp, i)), 'Method', 'Bag', 'NumLearningCycles', 10);
    pEns = predict(mEns, X(test(cvp, i), :));
    accEns(i) = mean(pEns == Y(test(cvp, i)));
end

% Calculate average accuracy across all 10 folds
meanAccTree = mean(accTree);
meanAccEns = mean(accEns);

% Display aggregated k-Fold cross-validation results
fprintf('\n== Results With 10-Fold Cross-Validation ==\n\n');
fprintf('Decision Tree Mean Accuracy: %.2f%%\n', meanAccTree * 100);
fprintf('Ensemble Learning Mean Accuracy: %.2f%%\n', meanAccEns * 100);

